From c820a1e82ec46b245959d34a036963fc721ea70c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:00:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: the feed applying our queued failure release
 clears the local claim; triage is a leftover-claim status

On a primary board the dead-worker sweep queues a run-scoped `release` command and leaves the
local row alone; the Board feed later moves the card off `running`. Claim columns are local-only,
so the feed never cleared them and the card kept the dead worker's claim_lock/worker_pid.

worker-7 fixture t_01a1d62545843356:
- run 2440 (rc=0 protocol violation) went `ready` but kept `claim_lock hermes-worker-7:2256394`
  until the leftover sweep released it after ORPHAN_CLAIM_GRACE_SECONDS (retry ~3.5 min late);
- run 2462 gave up to `triage` and kept its claim forever (`triage` was missing from
  `_LEFTOVER_CLAIM_STATUSES`), so the creator's kanban_archive was refused "it is claimed".

Five whys: the claim stayed -> the feed only writes synced columns -> the release is applied by
the Board, not by the local sweep (by design: no provisional mirror edits) -> nothing tied the
feed's status move to the local claim the release was about -> the leftover sweep was the only
backstop, gated by a grace window and a status list that omitted triage.

Fix:
1. `kanban_release_claim.release_on_feed`, called from `_upsert_task` in the same feed apply
   transaction: when the card leaves `running`, the claim is this host's, its claimed run has a
   `kanban_failure_commands` row this host queued (worker already judged gone) and the worker is
   not alive, clear claim_lock/claim_expires/worker_pid/worker_started_at/last_heartbeat_at
   (CAS on the exact values read). Covers ready (retry), triage/blocked (give-up) and the neutral
   releases that use the same command table.
2. `triage` added to `_LEFTOVER_CLAIM_STATUSES` as the backstop.

Tests:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_release_claim.py: the real primary crash sweep with an rc=0
  protocol violation, then the Board's feed row: ready/triage/blocked each leave claim_lock NULL
  in the same apply; the triage card is archivable by its creator; controls: a status move with
  no queued release, a live worker, and a feed row still `running` keep the claim.
  RED without the fix: 5 failed (claim kept, "it is claimed (status=triage)").
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_leftover_local_claim.py: the status sweep covers triage
  (RED without the fix: test_every_non_running_status_is_covered[triage] fails).
